# run: b3-diagnose
# seasons: 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025
# seeds: 60  seat: 6
# units: 6000  wall: 360.4s
#
# OUTCOME MEASURE:
#   points-for under a PRIOR lineup: the season lineup is
#   chosen on a (position, positional rank) table fitted
#   leave-one-season-out, so no information about the season
#   being scored reaches it
#   TWO UPPER BOUNDS are printed beside every comparison. An
#   `oracle` lineup chosen on each player's own season mean
#   is worth +90 to +107 points a season over the prior; a
#   `hindsight` lineup chosen weekly is worth +353 to +392.
#   Any effect smaller than that spread is inside the
#   harness's own uncertainty about what a manager could
#   have known, and is not a result.
#
# THE BASELINE, and read this before anything else:
#   audible against a ten-line ADP-greedy seat with no
#   audible in it at all, paired: +5.5 [-36.4, +47.4].
#   audible does NOT beat the obvious alternative.
#
# HOW MUCH ORDERING IS THERE ON THE ADP-ORDERED BOARD
# that real/shuffle/legacy/the ablations draft off? none:
#   2021: 128/128 exact, 0 disagree >1rd, r=1.0
#   2022: 128/128 exact, 0 disagree >1rd, r=1.0
#   2023: 128/128 exact, 0 disagree >1rd, r=1.0
#   2024: 128/128 exact, 0 disagree >1rd, r=1.0
#   2025: 128/128 exact, 0 disagree >1rd, r=1.0
#   the harness board is a monotone transform of ADP rank,
#   so its ordering IS the market's. real - adp therefore
#   measures the OVERLAY alone, never the board.
#   production espn_davis_drive:
#     6/128 exact, 72 disagree >1rd, r=0.8925
#   production espn_green_hope:
#     3/128 exact, 100 disagree >1rd, r=0.7167
#   the production board disagrees with ADP across most of
#   the top 128. That disagreement is where audible's value
#   would live and this harness cannot exercise it.
#
# advantage over the field, paired, clustered on season:
#   adp         +134.2 [+120.7, +147.8]
#   bot         -9.6 [-39.7, +20.6]
#   legacy      +154.6 [+95.1, +214.1]
#   legacy_recommend +128.4 [+116.5, +140.3]
#   no_bye      +138.9 [+92.0, +185.8]
#   no_need     +156.9 [+132.0, +181.9]
#   no_slice    +130.9 [+85.8, +175.9]
#   no_urgency  +132.0 [+91.0, +173.0]
#   real        +139.7 [+103.9, +175.6]
#   shuffle     +47.8 [+10.2, +85.5]
#
# paired comparisons. PRIOR is primary; the lines
# under each say what an oracle lineup would have paid:
#   real - adp: +5.5 [-36.4, +47.4]
#     oracle: +2.1 [-35.4, +39.5]
#     hindsight: -15.9 [-51.3, +19.5]
#   real - legacy: -14.9 [-77.1, +47.3]
#     oracle: -15.7 [-70.9, +39.6]
#     hindsight: -27.1 [-71.2, +17.0]
#   legacy - adp: +20.4 [-51.2, +92.0]
#     oracle: +17.7 [-27.3, +62.8]
#     hindsight: +11.2 [-31.1, +53.5]
